 "card": {
  "who": "Father Walsh's housekeeper. She shops the market, queues at Laverack's and takes tea at the Copper Kettle, and brings home every word.",
  "speak": "Chatty, pious in passing, fond of a \"God love him\". Never unkind to a face.",
  "life": "Kept the presbytery twenty-two years. Knows who was at Mass and who was not.",
  "fire": "She lit a candle for whoever did it, which Father says is the right way round.",
  "rivals": "Mrs Jensen gives to the roof fund. Mr Agar gives more and wants it read out."
 },
